From b83c65cd1432e435e00987e8e2971ce605bdb2e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Gilbertson <880013+gilby@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 4 Jul 2026 23:50:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] DeepSeek-V4-Flash enablement layer for DGX Spark
 (GB10/sm_121a), TP2

The 0.24 base ships the native deepseek_v4 package but cannot serve it on
GB10. This layer fixes the full cascade, validated end-to-end on 2x DGX
Spark over RoCE (TP2 + expert parallel):

- pin nvidia-cutlass-dsl 4.5.2: 4.6.0 removed cute.core.ThrMma, which the
  base's own fused_indexer_q_cutedsl.py still uses (breaks any DSv4 load)
- DeepGEMM nv_dev @ a6b593d (deepseek-ai/DeepGEMM#324): native sm120
  kernels for fp8_einsum / tf32_hc_prenorm_gemm / paged mqa logits
- flashinfer 0.6.14: the swa_topk_lens sparse-MLA decode API the base's
  flashinfer_sparse.py already targets (image shipped 0.6.12)
- sm12x-gated overlays: o_proj adapter to the nv_dev einsum API (unpacked
  fp32 scales, 3D weights), persistent_topk instead of cooperative_topk
  (cluster launch fails on GB10), exact e8m0->fp32 triton scale upcast
- serve recipe: marlin MoE + triton linear, VLLM_DEEP_GEMM_WARMUP=skip,
  --enforce-eager --max-num-seqs 2 (batched long-context decode wedges
  under every cudagraph mode on GB10 -- documented as a known issue)

Validation: full 12-category multi-turn benchmark, 48/48 turns, zero
engine errors; 17.8 tok/s single-stream, 28.6 tok/s aggregate; output
quality graded at parity with the independent jasl-fork GB10 build;
temp-0 probes numerically consistent with that build.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
